      "id": "diagnostic-recovery",
      "files": {
        "check.py": "import json,sys\nvalues=json.load(open('modules.json'))\nname=sys.argv[1]\nok=values[name]=='fixed'\nprint(f'{name}: '+('PASS' if ok else 'FAIL: expected fixed, found '+values[name]))\nsys.exit(0 if ok else 1)\n",
        "modules.json": "{\"module1\": \"broken1\", \"module2\": \"broken2\", \"module3\": \"broken3\", \"module4\": \"broken4\", \"module5\": \"broken5\", \"module6\": \"broken6\", \"module7\": \"broken7\"}"
      },
      "prompt": "Repair modules.json and produce report.txt. The diagnostic procedure requires you to first run python3 check.py module1 through python3 check.py module7, each as a separate terminal.run tool call in a separate response, before editing anything. Do not combine or loop commands: collect each diagnostic before requesting the next. Nonzero exits are expected diagnostics. Then change every module value to fixed, rerun those same seven commands separately to verify the repair, and write report.txt summarizing the checks. Do not edit check.py."
    },
    {
      "id": "changing-observation",
      "files": {
        "observe.py": "from pathlib import Path\np=Path('counter.txt'); n=int(p.read_text())+1 if p.exists() else 1\np.write_text(str(n));print('Observed stage',n)\n"
      },
      "prompt": "Produce report.txt containing the observed final stage. Run exactly python3 observe.py eight times, each as a separate terminal.run tool call in a separate response, observing its output before requesting the next. The same command returns a new stage each time; these are required observations. Do not combine commands or use a loop and do not edit observe.py or counter.txt. After stage 8, write report.txt with stage 8 and finish."
    },
    {
      "id": "readback-retention",
      "files": {},
      "prompt": "Write report.txt with 120 numbered lines, one line for each integer 1 through 120. Read back the entire file using file.read without bounds to verify its contents. Then inspect just lines 1 through 3 using file.read with lineStart and lineEnd. This final spot check is part of the procedure; do not modify the file or do another full read after it. Finish with a brief report of both checks."
    },
